      "value": "None"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "For a low-dimensional subspace (e.g., constraints defining a line or plane in function space), we expect $N_c(w)$ to plateau at a small finite value (e.g., $N_c \\approx 5-20$) as $w$ increases up to the subspace dimension. The maximum test error should drop below $10^{-3}$ once $N \\ge N_c(w)$ and remain there. If the subspace is truly low-dimensional, the curve $N_c(w)$ vs $w$ will be flat until $w$ exceeds the intrinsic dimension, after which $N_c(w)$ may increase."
